# Test: the rendering key hands over presentation only, never selection
#
# The one question (security negative): when an SSH client sets the session
# rendering key and sends `monitor ... | match state`, does the daemon still
# apply `match`, so the client receives no line the chain removes; is a value
# of the key other than the defined one refused by name before any command
# runs; and does the key on a one-shot exec change nothing? The unit tests
# (TestRenderingKeyNeverSkipsSelection, TestRenderingKeyUnknownValueRefused,
# TestRenderingKeyIgnoredOnOneShotExec) prove each arm in process; only a
# daemon proves the exec channel reads the key the way an outside client
# sends it.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-pipe-chain-honored-on-every-command-surface AC-36, AC-37,
#   R-12, user story 12.
# PREVENTS: the key read as permission: a client that sets it receiving the
#   rows a `| match` the authorizer judged would have removed.
#
# The key: sshclient.EnvCLIRender = "ZE_CLI_RENDER", its one value
# CLIRenderClient = "client" (internal/component/cli/sshclient/terminal.go),
# read by parseSessionRequest (internal/component/ssh/session.go).
#
# Red at 5ebf3c1c8e (run 2026-11-20 19:20): seq 2's stream ended after the
#   header. With the key the daemon applies `match` alone, over raw events,
#   where it refuses an OPEN event as one document (read, not observed: the
#   run's stderr was lost, see below), the same fault
#   monitor-pipe-chain-ssh.ci met (fixed by applyEventMatch,
#   internal/component/command/pipe.go). The fixture printed an empty stderr
#   because it read the session's stderr before the session's copy of it
#   finished; it now waits for the session first (ssh_exec_line.go ended).
#
# Method: monitor-pipe-chain-ssh.ci's daemon, with a local user instead of
# TACACS+, driven by internal/test/fixture plugin/ssh-exec-line, which sets
# each KEY=VALUE argument on the session before the exec.

option=timeout:value=60s

tmpfs=monitor.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
			profile [ admin ]
		}
	}
	authorization {
		profile admin { run { default-action allow; } edit { default-action allow; } }
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT2;
		}
	}
}
bgp {
	group dynamic-monitor {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip dynamic
				connect false
				range 127.0.0.1/32
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				port $PORT3
				accept true
			}
		}
		session {
			asn { local 65000; }
			router-id 1.1.1.1
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability { graceful-restart disable; }
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start monitor.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

# AC-36: the key set; `match state` still runs in the daemon, so no OPEN
# event reaches the client. The `| save` of the AC needs a client that
# writes files and is cli-monitor-pipe-typed-line.ci's question.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture plugin/ssh-exec-line stream $PORT2 $PORT3 'monitor event include open,state | match state' up open ZE_CLI_RENDER=client:timeout=45s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: monitor event include open,state | match state printed up and no line holding open

# AC-37: a value other than the defined one is refused by name, before any
# command runs: the header of the monitor never prints.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture plugin/ssh-exec-line refused $PORT2 - 'monitor event include state' ZE_CLI_RENDER monitoring ZE_CLI_RENDER=everything:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: monitor event include state refused, naming ZE_CLI_RENDER

# AC-37: on a one-shot exec the key changes nothing: the daemon renders the
# whole chain, so the answer is the count document, not rows.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=le test fixture plugin/ssh-exec-line once $PORT2 - 'system command list | count | json' count - ZE_CLI_RENDER=client:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:pattern=ssh-exec: .*"count": ?[1-9]

cmd=stop:seq=5:name=daemon:signal=term
